- op: discuss  # 548f
  at: '2026-07-05T08:37:49Z'  # 548f
  by: agent  # 548f
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 548f
  clock: 3  # 548f
  nonce: 548f  # 548f
  message: "Fixed jointly with INV-fihur in PR (dev abf47e01a7). Root cause: nim.py _extract_import_edges emitted a malformed 4-slot import dst nim:?:{module}:module — a '?' placeholder in the path slot, no span. refine_frameworks reads the imported module as edge.dst.split(':')[1] (the path slot) -> it saw '?'; and _parse_dangling_id (needs 5 colon-parts) fell back to module_path/src = the <unknown> sentinel. So every Nim import was invisible to framework refinement -> jester/karax false-demoted on nitter. Fix: emit the canonical nim:{module}:0-0:module:module form (mirrors py.py's python:{module}:0-0:module:module), module in parts[1]; both the plain-identifier and infix-module code paths. Behavioral evidence (analyze_nim): import jester -> nim:jester:0-0:module:module (parts[1]='jester', was '?'). Extended package 100% coverage."  # 548f
